                'boundary':'Actual CLI dispatch and standard adapters. Passing an arbitrary fabricated NaN object through a monkeypatched dispatch would violate this caller invariant and is not an equivalence proof counterexample.','callers':['mutation.dispatch→run_mutation→shared_runner.read_json→shared_mutation.assess→mutation.main']}
    if name=='add_details':
        return {'classification':'equivalent','kind':'stable-mutmut-path-resolution','byteEquivalent':True,'reasoning':'The pinned mutmut 3.8.0 default is literally if path is None: path=find_mutant(mutant_name).path. add_details has just called the same resolver with the same ID; intervening function_position only parses the original source and does not change cwd, configuration, metadata or the key. In the synchronous completed-run analysis copy both lookups therefore select the same first match and the same get_diff implementation/index fallback. Missing IDs fail at the first lookup in both. Class names, dotted module keys, Unicode filenames and file-name case do not change this argument because the lookup input is identical, not reconstructed. The variant performs an extra metadata scan, so this is output/error equivalence rather than identical I/O cost.',
                'boundary':'Pinned mutmut 3.8.0, single-threaded exporter after completed engine run, unchanged cwd/config/source/metadata during extraction. Concurrent external alteration of metadata or global cwd is not protected by either version; no universal equivalence claim across such races.','callers':['lang_python.main after subprocess mutmut completion'],
