        return {'classification':'equivalent_with_memory_boundary','kind':'reachable-in-memory-utf16-bound','byteEquivalent':True,'reasoning':'Its sole source_offset caller passes a list of built-in str lines from parsed JSON source and integer coordinates. UTF-16LE yields a real bytes allocation of even length L. For any allocation with L/2+1 representable exactly in binary64, integer division and float division produce the same comparison bound. Real source allocations on the repository supported hosts are far below 2**54 bytes, so the path has no reachable differing coordinate. This is explicitly not an unconditional arithmetic identity: L=2**54 and column=2**53+1 makes the integer bound accept and the rounded float bound reject. Producing that real encoded line needs at least 16 PiB for this one bytes object; a fake object with a custom __len__ is not reachable from JSON strings.',
